},{\"f\":300,\"location\":[-0.327,-7.562,5.633],\"target\":[-0.322,1.256,0.917],\"roll_deg\":-1.33,\"lens_mm\":36.0},{\"f\":301,\"location\":[-0.311,-7.566,5.628],\"target\":[-0.316,1.252,0.913],\"roll_deg\":-1.3,\"lens_mm\":36.0},{\"f\":302,\"location\":[-0.311,-7.566,5.628],\"target\":[-0.316,1.252,0.913],\"roll_deg\":-1.3,\"lens_mm\":36.0},{\"f\":303,\"location\":[-0.292,-7.572,5.622],\"target\":[-0.307,1.25,0.911],\"roll_deg\":-1.25,\"lens_mm\":36.0}],\"dof\":{\"enabled\":true,\"focus\":[0.12,0.41,1.4],\"fstop\":2.8,\"focus_keys\":[{\"f\":149,\"focus\":[-0.58,-6.67,5.38]},{\"f\":176,\"focus\":[-0.58,-6.67,5.38]},{\"f\":200,\"focus\":[0.12,0.41,1.4]},{\"f\":303,\"focus\":[0.12,0.41,1.4]}],\"note\":\"rack focus: DS hair sharp f149-176 (bow Laplacian var ~300), background sharp from f197-201; interpolate focus distance 0.6 m -> 8.9 m over f177-200. f/2.8 at 36 mm reproduces the ~40-55 px lamp bokeh discs of f150.\"}}],\"markers\":[{\"f\":149,\"name\":\"S2_start_OTS_behind_DS_head\"},{\"f\":177,\"name\":\"S2_focus_pull_start\"},{\"f\":198,\"name\":\"S2_CL_clear_of_DS_shoulder\"},{\"f\":200,\"name\":\"S2_focus_on_crowd_CL\"},{\"f\":258,\"name\":\"S2_DS_bow_leaves_frame\"},{\"f\":303,\"name\":\"S2_end\"}],\"notes\":[\"SHOT 2 CAMERA: 36 mm (f=1920 px, vFOV 53.1 deg) fixed lens, keyed every frame (f%5==2 duplicates repeat f-1). Move = mostly ROTATION: pan left 16.1 deg (yaw 16.1 -> 0), tilt down 5.1 deg (pitch 22.96 -> 28.10), roll +1.66 -> -1.25 deg, plus a short arc of the camera body 0.46 m to +X, 0.34 m to -Y, 0.17 m up (over DS's right shoulder). That small translation is what slides DS's head ~1100 px left relative to the background; it is invisible on the crowd.\",\"The ORB-based 'push x1.15 / roll +12 deg / drift 390 px' in measured.json is NOT the camera: before f200 its features sit on DS's sharp hair and after that on dancing crowd. Static table lamps tracked through all 124 unique frames give background scale x1.03, image rotation +3.45 deg (clockwise; mostly the pan of a down-tilted camera), centre shift (+431, -167) px; CL's anime-face box stays 54+-2 px from f200 to f303 (no push).\",\"Venue implied by the shot-2 view (z=0 pit floor): camera f303 at (-0.29,-7.57,5.62) i.e. 5.62 m above the pit, 7.58 m horizontally from the stage centre; DS's VIP balcony floor z=4.0 at Y~-7 with a diagonal (-28.8 deg) chrome/glass balustrade; far mezzanine fascia (z 3.65-4.45) at Y~12 with 1.1 m glass balustrade; right side gallery edge running from (5.6,12) towards (3.0,-4) (heading ~9 deg off the Y axis); back tiers from Y~5.5; crowd visible on the pit from Y~-5 (bottom of frame) to Y~6.\",\"CL position cheat: the lit disc centre (origin) is 0.55 m in front of CL's feet; placing CL at the origin misses the head-blob anchors by ~51 px (mean). The overhead beam (visible top-centre, x~640 @f303) is consistent with a near-vertical spot from ~7 m above CL aimed at the disc centre.\",\"Background depth cheat: a lamp-only parallax solve wants the table lamps at only 8-13 m (same depth as CL); with tables placed coherently on tiers 13-25 m away the early defocused frames f149-200 drift up to ~15-25 px (median), f250-303 < 7 px. The camera keys are from the joint solve (lamps 1.6 px, CL 6.4 px, DS bow 1-3 px through f230).\"]}", "measurements": [{"name": "shot2_lens", "value": "36 mm (f=1920 px, vFOV 53.1 deg); fit 1914+-180 px => ~32-40 mm; constant (no zoom)", "unit": "mm", "method": "Joint least squares at f303: pooled nadir vanishing point (789 near-vertical LSD segments over f225-303 mapped to f303 coordinates), head-top/foot pairs of 3 standing figures (two crowd women at 1.65 m, CL at 1.60 m), 18 crowd head widths (0.185 m) against image row, and a cocktail-table ellipse. A bundle-adjustment cost scan over f=1500-2600 px favours 1900-2600 px.", "confidence": 0.6}, {"name": "shot2_camera_f303_pose", "value": "location (-0.29,-7.57,5.62); yaw 0 (looks along +Y), pitch (optical-axis depression) 28.1 deg, roll -1.25 deg", "unit": "m / deg", "method": "Metrology fit (above) for pitch, roll and height. XY is set so the lit-disc centre seen in the f240-303 aligned 85th-percentile composite (607,1245) lands on the origin. Yaw comes from the far mezzanine fascia, which stays parallel to image horizontal after the roll (-1.7 vs -1.1 deg).", "confidence": 0.6}, {"name": "camera_height_above_pit_f303", "value": "5.62 (+-0.3; scales with the assumed 1.65 m crowd height); 5.57 above the disc top; 1.62 above DS balcony floor", "unit": "m", "method": "Single-view metrology: heights of standing figures from head/feet pairs with the fitted f and pitch", "confidence": 0.55}, {"name": "horizontal_distance_camera_to_stage_centre_f303", "value": "7.58 (to CL's feet 8.13; 3D distance to CL head 9.0)", "unit": "m", "method": "Ray to the disc-centre image point intersected with z=0 for the fitted camera", "confidence": 0.6}, {"name": "elevation_angles", "value": "optical axis 22.96 deg down at f149, 28.10 deg at f303; line of sight to stage centre 36.6 deg down; to CL head 27 deg down", "unit": "deg", "method": "From the solved camera keys", "confidence": 0.7}, {"name": "stage_disc_ellipse", "value": "lit pool spans x 452-762 (310 px wide), bottom edge y~1332, widest at y~1230-1260 at f303; minor/major ~0.56-0.6; a disc of r=0.8 m at the origin projects to ratio 0.60", "unit": "px / ratio", "method": "Lit floor edges read on a gridded zoom of the 85th-percentile composite of 52 frames (f240-303), each aligned to f303 by the lamp similarity chain (dancers average out). Projected ellipses for r=0.8/0.95/1.1 were overlaid.", "confidence": 0.6}, {"name": "stage_disc_radius", "value": "0.8 (+-0.1)", "unit": "m", "method": "Overlay of projected circles on the composite; the r=0.8 left, right and bottom points sit within 12-20 px of the lit-pool edges", "confidence": 0.55}, {"name": "nadir_vanishing_point_f303", "value": "(607, 4493) +-(7,122) bootstrap => roll -1.09 deg, f/tan(pitch)=3534 px", "unit": "px", "method": "Robust (soft-L1) VP fit to near-vertical LSD segments (glass joints, mezzanine columns), pooled over f225-303 and mapped to f303 coordinates", "confidence": 0.65}, {"name": "background_motion_over_shot2", "value": "scale x1.032, rotation +3.45 deg (clockwise), image-centre shift (+431,-167) px from f149 to f303", "unit": "ratio / deg / px", "method": "White lamp cores detected (min channel >228, plus warm bokeh blobs before f200), with 54 consistent tracks; similarity transforms fitted between consecutive unique frames and chained. Cross-checked by direct fits f225/240/260 -> f303.", "confidence": 0.85}, {"name": "camera_rotation_shot2", "value": "yaw 16.1 -> 0 deg (pan left 16.1), pitch 22.96 -> 28.10 (tilt down 5.1), roll +1.66 -> -1.25 deg; most of the tilt happens f230-303 and the pan is front-loaded (yaw 7.1 at f200, 1.5 at f250)", "unit": "deg", "method": "Sparse bundle adjustment over 124 unique frames: 6-DoF camera per frame with a smoothness prior, free lamp 3D points, fixed CL head point, DS bow point with a 0.6 m distance prior, and the handrail line. Positions were then Savitzky-Golay smoothed (window 15) and rotations re-fitted per frame.", "confidence": 0.7}, {"name": "camera_translation_shot2", "value": "+0.46 X, -0.34 Y, +0.17 Z over f149->303 (arc over DS's right shoulder); background-only data allow 0-0.45 m", "unit": "m", "method": "Required by the parallax of DS's right hair bow, template-tracked f150-258 (moves 733 px left while the background moves 409 px right). The background alone (lamps + CL) fits a pure rotation equally well: rotation-only CL residual <=18 px.", "confidence": 0.45}, {"name": "ORB_push_roll_artifact", "value": "measured.json zoom 1.146 / roll 12.15 / pan (-70,-391) for shot 2 does not describe the camera; background zoom is 1.03, image rotation 3.45 deg, shift (+431,-167)", "unit": "", "method": "Compared against lamp tracks and against CL's anime-face box, which stays 54+-2 px over f200-303. Masked SIFT bands (tables, mid crowd,